  "configuration_id": "config_022",
  "reason": "With zero completed experiments, the most critical uncertainty is establishing a performance floor for the RNA modality alone, which serves as the reference against which all multimodal, multiprofile, and learned-encoder choices will be judged. config_022 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest possible RNA baseline: a well-understood linear encoder (PCA), no multi-profile aggregation, no image branch, and no fusion step. This isolates the raw signal quality of the RNA data with minimal confounding from learned representations or architectural complexity. It directly tests whether a basic RNA-only model achieves competitive accuracy, which is essential before investing budget in more complex multimodal or multiprofile variants. Under a limited budget, anchoring the search with a clean, interpretable baseline is the highest-information first step: it calibrates expectations, reveals whether the task is already solvable with simple features, and provides a clear ablation target for every subsequent experiment."
}

